<article class="env-lemma" id="03KL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03KL">Lemma <span data-tag="03KL">67.4.4</span>.</a> All of the separation axioms listed in Definition <a href="/tag/03HL" data-tag="03HL">67.4.2</a> are stable under base change. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to Y$ and $Y' \to Y$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces. Let $f' : X' \to Y'$ be the base change of $f$ by $Y' \to Y$. Then $\Delta _{X'/Y'}$ is the base change of $\Delta _{X/Y}$ by the morphism $X' \times _{Y'} X' \to X \times _ Y X$. By the results of Section <a href="/tag/03HA" data-tag="03HA">67.3</a> each of the properties of the diagonal used in Definition <a href="/tag/03HL" data-tag="03HL">67.4.2</a> is stable under base change. Hence the lemma is true. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>